  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Cool mornings and pleasant afternoons the rest of the week.\n\n- Gusty winds and choppy lakes on Saturday, especially across\n  northwest MT.\n\n- Pattern shift early next week, gradually cooling and a chance \n  of showers. \n\nHigh pressure will bring mostly sunny skies and pleasant mid-October\nweather across the region through Friday, aside from some patchy \nmorning valley fog. High temperatures on Friday may be slightly \ncooler in the valleys than some forecast models suggest due to \nstable conditions and stubborn nighttime inversions. \n\nThe pattern shifts on Saturday as a dry cold front sweeps through\nwestern Montana and north-central Idaho by the evening. Ahead of \nthe front, breezy westerly winds will help warm daytime \ntemperatures. Expect surface wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph, with \nexposed higher terrain seeing gusts near 50 mph. These winds will \ncreate choppy conditions on local lakes and pose hazards for small\nwatercraft. While a few light showers may clip northwest Montana,\nprecipitation will be negligible. Cooler air arrives Sunday \nbehind the front, though temperatures will still remain slightly \nabove normal for this time of year.\n\nBy early next week, a broader weather system will move into the \nwestern US, bringing a shift toward a more active pattern. While \nthe most significant moisture and storm energy are expected to \ntrack well south of our area into the Great Basin, the Northern \nRockies will still transition to a more unsettled regime. Expect a\nreturn of precipitation chances and a cool down to near-average \nseasonal temperatures.",
